  "rationale": "TUBB3-2A-mCherry dCas9-VP64 iPSCs, single-factor CRISPRa screen (1,496 TFs, ~5 guides each, 100 scrambled controls), sorted into mCherry-low and mCherry-high bins after 4-5 days; guides activating neurogenic TFs are enriched in mCherry-high cells. The paper called TFs with two or more guides enriched (DESeq2 FDR < 0.01) in mCherry-high relative to both the unsorted and the mCherry-low bins. The primary contrast is mCherry-high versus mCherry-low; each replicate's bins come from one independent transduction, so replicate is a blocking term (2 residual df). Column names give bin and replicate and match the GSM titles; the gene is the guide id without its '.N' suffix (prepare.R).",
